Testing a Reform The college wanted to enhance teaching and diminish paperwork

2
00:00:06,368 --> 00:00:11,342
A radical proposal promised a decisive improvement but critics feared instability and

3
00:00:11,355 --> 00:00:16,789
the consequent confusion Its inherent drawback was the time required for training

4
00:00:17,697 --> 00:00:22,026
The committee chose to subdivide the project and test one stage experimentally

5
00:00:22,934 --> 00:00:26,711
This would not constitute a perfect comparison but it could reveal a

6
00:00:26,724 --> 00:00:33,605
complication early A clear procedure would precede each change Staff would consolidate

7
00:00:33,618 --> 00:00:38,816
initial gains and offset extra work with additional support The question was

8
00:00:38,829 --> 00:00:44,289
whether the reform could operate economically A resolute commitment to improvement can

9
00:00:44,303 --> 00:00:47,921
coexist with a willingness to reverse a decision when its effects prove

10
00:00:47,934 --> 00:00:48,816
